Build me a complete n8n workflow JSON from this spec. If anything is ambiguous, ask me — but keep building your best-guess version while you wait, don't stop.

Attached file "payment-flow-spec.json" (application/json):
```
{
  "goal": "When a Stripe payment succeeds, upsert the customer in HubSpot, then post a summary to #finance in Slack. On amounts over $5,000 also email the CFO.",
  "triggers": [
    "stripe payment_intent.succeeded"
  ],
  "systems": {
    "crm": "HubSpot",
    "chat": "Slack",
    "email": "SMTP (Office 365)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "dedupe customers by email",
    "Slack message must include amount, customer name, product",
    "retry failed HubSpot calls 3 times"
  ]
}
```

I'll build you a complete n8n workflow JSON. I'm asking one quick clarification while I work:

**Clarification needed:**
- In Stripe's `payment_intent`, product info typically isn't included. Should I pull it from:
  - The `metadata` field (you'll set it there)?
  - The related `invoice` object?
  - A static fallback (e.g., "Product Sale")?

I'll assume **metadata** for now and you can override.

---

Here's your workflow:

<protean:artefact type="code" title="Stripe Payment → HubSpot + Slack + Email (n8n)">
{
  "name": "Stripe Payment to CRM and Notifications",
  "description": "Upsert HubSpot contact on Stripe payment_intent.succeeded, post to Slack, email CFO if > $5000",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "events": "payment_intent.succeeded"
      },
      "id": "stripe-webhook",
      "name": "Stripe Payment Succeeded",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stripeWebhookTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [250, 300],
      "webhookId": "stripe_payment_succeeded"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "combine",
        "assignments": [
          {
            "name": "amountCents",
            "value": "={{ $json.data.object.amount }}"
          },
          {
            "name": "amountUSD",
            "value": "={{ ($json.data.object.amount / 100).toFixed(2) }}"
          },
          {
            "name": "customerEmail",
            "value": "={{ $json.data.object.billing_details?.email || $json.data.object.receipt_email }}"
          },
          {
            "name": "customerName",
            "value": "={{ $json.data.object.billing_details?.name || 'Unknown' }}"
          },
          {
            "name": "productDescription",
            "value": "={{ $json.data.object.metadata?.product || 'Premium Subscription' }}"
          },
          {
            "name": "paymentId",
            "value": "={{ $json.data.object.id }}"
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "extract-payment",
      "name": "Extract Payment Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [500, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "contact",
        "operation": "upsert",
        "email": "={{ $json.customerEmail }}",
        "additionalFields": {
          "properties": [
            {
              "name": "firstname",
              "value": "={{ $json.customerName.split(' ')[0] }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "lastname",
              "value": "={{ $json.customerName.split(' ').slice(1).join(' ') || '' }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "hs_lead_status",
              "value": "customer"
            },
            {
              "name": "lifecyclestage",
              "value": "customer"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "hubspot-upsert",
      "name": "HubSpot Upsert Contact (Retry 3×)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.hubspot",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [750, 300],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxRetries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 2,
      "credentials": {
        "hubspotApi": "hubspot-oauth-connection"
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "channel": "#finance",
        "text": "💳 **Payment Received**\n\n💰 *Amount:* $${{ $json.amountUSD }}\n👤 *Customer:* ${{ $json.customerName }}\n📦 *Product:* ${{ $json.productDescription }}\n🆔 *Payment ID:* `${{ $json.paymentId }}`",
        "otherOptions": {}
      },
      "id": "slack-notify",
      "name": "Post to Slack #finance",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [1000, 300],
      "credentials": {
        "slackApi": "slack-webhook-or-oauth"
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "number": [
            {
              "value1": "={{ $json.amountCents }}",
              "value2": 500000,
              "operation": ">"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "check-amount-5000",
      "name": "Is amount > $5,000?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [1250, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "protocol": "smtp",
        "host": "smtp.office365.com",
        "port": 587,
        "user": "={{ $env.OFFICE365_EMAIL }}",
        "password": "={{ $env.OFFICE365_PASSWORD }}",
        "toEmail": "={{ $env.CFO_EMAIL }}",
        "subject": "🚨 High-Value Payment: $${{ $json.amountUSD }} from ${{ $json.customerName }}",
        "textOnly": false,
        "html": true,
        "htmlMessage": "<h2>High-Value Payment Alert</h2><p><strong>Amount:</strong> $${{ $json.amountUSD }}</p><p><strong>Customer:</strong> ${{ $json.customerName }} (${{ $json.customerEmail }})</p><p><strong>Product:</strong> ${{ $json.productDescription }}</p><p><strong>Payment ID:</strong> ${{ $json.paymentId }}</p><p>Please review in HubSpot for further action.</p>",
        "tlsOption": "require"
      },
      "id": "email-cfo",
      "name": "Email CFO via Office 365 SMTP",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.emailSendSMTP",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1500, 200],
      "credentials": {
        "smtp": "office365-smtp"
      },
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "end-node",
      "name": "Workflow Complete",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1500, 400]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Stripe Payment Succeeded": [
      {
        "node": "Extract Payment Data",
        "type": "main",
        "index": [0, 0]
      }
    ],
    "Extract Payment Data": [
      {
        "node": "HubSpot Upsert Contact (Retry 3×)",
        "type": "main",
        "index": [0, 0]
      }
    ],
    "HubSpot Upsert Contact (Retry 3×)": [
      {
        "node": "Post to Slack #finance",
        "type": "main",
        "index": [0, 0]
      }
    ],
    "Post to Slack #finance": [
      {
        "node": "Is amount > $5,000?",
        "type": "main",
        "index": [0, 0]
      }
    ],
    "Is amount > $5,000?": [
      {
        "node": "Email CFO via Office 365 SMTP",
        "type": "main",
        "index": [0, 0]
      },
      {
        "node": "Workflow Complete",
        "type": "main",
        "index": [0, 1]
      }
    ],
    "Email CFO via Office 365 SMTP": [
      {
        "node": "Workflow Complete",
        "type": "main",
        "index": [0, 0]
      }
    ]
  },
  "settings": {
    "saveManualExecutions": true,
    "executionOrder": "v1",
    "errorHandler": {
      "type": "simple"
    }
  },
  "versionId": "1"
}
</protean:artefact>

---

## **Key build details:**

| Feature | Implementation |
|---------|-----------------|
| **Dedupe by email** | HubSpot `upsert` + `email` field naturally dedupes |
| **Retry logic** | `retryOnFail: true`, `maxRetries: 3`, `waitBetweenTries: 2s` |
| **Slack message** | Formatted with amount, customer name, product, payment ID |
| **Conditional email** | IF node: `amountCents > 500000` (500,000¢ = $5,000) |
| **SMTP (Office 365)** | Uses `smtp.office365.com:587` + TLS; credentials from env vars |
| **Error handling** | CFO email has `onError: continueRegularOutput` so workflow doesn't fail if email fails |

## **Setup checklist:**

1. **Stripe webhook:** n8n will generate a unique webhook URL—add it to your Stripe dashboard under Webhooks (listen for `payment_intent.succeeded`)
2. **Credentials needed:**
   - HubSpot OAuth token
   - Slack webhook or OAuth
   - Office 365 email + password (store in n8n Credentials as `OFFICE365_EMAIL`, `OFFICE365_PASSWORD`, `CFO_EMAIL`)
3. **Stripe metadata:** Set `metadata.product = "Your Product Name"` when creating the payment_intent, or the workflow defaults to "Premium Subscription"

**What's still ambiguous:**
- Should I fetch the product from Stripe's related invoice/line items instead of metadata?
- Do you want separate error logging node, or is the existing error handling sufficient?
- CFO email—should it be a fixed env var or looked up from HubSpot?

Keep building, or tell me and I'll adjust.

